Build the stability-milestone pruner — the convergence lever for cross-project vision debt, and the documented exit condition for scheduler+realisateur's weight-3 bump in scheduler/schedule/_paced.conf. Two parts: (a) a per-project stability-milestone convention (a data shape / FOCUS.md field marking 'the current milestone we're stabilizing toward'), and (b) realisateur's triage default-PARKS ideas that land past the current milestone, rather than folding them into the active queue. Decided in scheduler /ideate 2026-07-24: intake stays FRICTIONLESS (scheduler -i unchanged) and ALL triage/parking happens downstream in realisateur. Rationale: quota (now Claude Max on primary) only raises the ceiling the backlog diverges under; pruning is the only thing that converges it (net accrual ~10/wk zero-cost vs clear ~2-4/wk). When (a)+(b) exist, drop scheduler+realisateur weights back toward 1. See scheduler DESIGN-NOTES.md 2026-07-23 + 2026-07-24 entries.
